<title>HONG KONG: SHK Prop in Ma Wan residential project.</title>
<headline>SHK Prop in Ma Wan residential project.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong government said on Monday it signed an agreement with Sun Hung Kai Properties Ltd to develop a site in Ma Wan, which will be developed into a new town to house more than 10,000 people by the year 2003.</p>
<p>A government spokesman said in a statement a 45-block housing estate, comprising 3,600 flats, would be developed on a 12.65 hectare site in the northeastern part of the island, which sits between Hong Kong's Tsing Yi and Lantau Island.</p>
<p>The statement also said about 341 village houses and 120 flats would be provided for the villagers and the fishermen currently residing there.</p>
</text>
